
 Inverted indexes (a.k.a. posting lists) are core data structures in search engines and database systems, where compression is crucial to reduce memory footprint and accelerate query processing. The key challenge lies in encoding a sorted list of integer identifiers in a compact, lossless form while supporting fast decoding. Motivated by recent studies on learned data structures, this work presents
